  "notes": [
    "The five player-count/language loader fragments fold into the data-owning TU: GetLanguageIndex, func_0200f2cc, SetNumPlayers and the two empty frame hooks join func_0200f13c/func_0200f220. Reverse source order emits the seven functions ROM-ascending. Oracle-verified 7/7 byte-exact before application.",
    "Hand-assembled, not generated by `tubuild.py create`: tu_map cannot segment arm9/main. The schema follows arm9/Graphics3D.",
    "No ROM name for this file: neither function has an SDK or RTTI name. The file takes its lowest function's name and stays under src/unnamed/arm9/0200 (tools/layout_check.py L3 wants an address stem there) until a name is recovered, as arm9/func_02073300 does. That is why the first function's legacy_source and the promoted source are the same path: tools/tu_promote.py moved the TU to src/unnamed/arm9/0200/unit0200f13c.cpp, and it was renamed onto the retired shard's path after.",
    "Both functions keep C linkage: d_s_entry_methods.cpp and d_s_mb.cpp declare them extern \"C\".",
    "intact-object: the TU owns the player count, the two per-language pointer tables and the five interleaved file-ID tables in .data 0x0208a0e0..0x0208a170. The pointer tables' targets (data_02096f08 etc., data_02098b58 etc.) are other ranges' bytes and stay extern."
  ],
